---
title: Issue page
layout: home
description: One issue, as it was sent — the number and the date above the title, the letter itself at the reading width, and the way to join at the end for whoever arrived from a link.
eyebrow: Collections · Newsletter
source: src/components/collection.css · content.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Newsletter · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1.5rem">
		{{#with demo.issues.[0]}}
		<header class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .75rem">
			<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
				<ol class="im-breadcrumb im-breadcrumb-chevron">
					<li><a href="/">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a></li>
					<li><a href="/collections/newsletter/">{{> "icons/mail"}}<span>Field Notes</span></a></li>
					<li><span aria-current="page">Issue {{n}}</span></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>
			<p class="im-caption">Issue {{n}} · {{date}}</p>
			<h1 class="im-posthero-title" style="font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 1.3rem + 2.2vw, 2.75rem)">{{title}}</h1>
			<p class="im-posthero-excerpt">{{text}}</p>
		</header>
		{{/with}}

		<nav class="im-seriesbar" aria-label="Issues">
			<p class="im-seriesbar-label"><strong>Issue 42 of 42</strong><a href="/collections/newsletter/">Field Notes</a></p>
			<div class="im-seriesbar-nav">
				<a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="/collections/newsletter/issue/">{{icon "arrow-left"}}Issue 041</a>
				<a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="/collections/newsletter/" aria-disabled="true">Latest</a>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush im-content-lede" data-im-zoom>
			<p>The site ran on a theme somebody else wrote, under a licence that forbids redistribution and modification for resale. Everything built on it was therefore unsellable — including the thing I was building.</p>
			<h2>What it cost</h2>
			<p>Six weeks, and a rule I now apply to everything: if I cannot answer <em>where did this file come from</em>, it does not ship.</p>
			<div class="kg-card kg-callout-card kg-callout-card-yellow"><div class="kg-callout-emoji">📮</div><div class="kg-callout-text">This is an ordinary post with an internal tag. It has a URL, it is in the RSS feed, and a search engine can read it — which a newsletter archive locked inside a mail provider is not.</div></div>
			<h2>What is next</h2>
			<p>Collections: the page-shapes a site is actually made of, each one a collection, a card and a page.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="im-postcta">
			<h2 class="im-postcta-title">Get the next one</h2>
			<p class="im-postcta-text">One email when something lands. Nothing else, ever.</p>
			{{> "components/subscribe" id="issue-email" button="Subscribe"}}
		</section>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="i-about">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="i-about">This issue</h2>
					<dl class="im-widget-facts">
						<dt>Number</dt><dd>042</dd>
						<dt>Sent</dt><dd>18 Sep 2026</dd>
						<dt>Words</dt><dd>1,240</dd>
						<dt>Opened</dt><dd>62%</dd>
					</dl>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="i-recent">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="i-recent">Recent issues <a href="/collections/newsletter/">All</a></h2>
					<ul class="im-widget-list im-widget-list-ranked">
						{{#each demo.issues}}<li><a href="/collections/newsletter/issue/">{{title}}<small>{{date}}</small></a></li>{{/each}}
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="i-join">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="i-join">Join</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">4,100 readers.</p>
					{{> "components/subscribe" id="issue-email-2" button="Join"}}
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>It is the post layout</h2>
		<p>An issue is a post: the <a href="/collections/post/single/">single layout</a> with its sidebar on, the same <code>im-content</code> canvas, the same rail. What it adds is the <strong>number and date above the title</strong> — an issue is navigated by number — and a <a href="/collections/post/single/#the-series-bar">series bar</a> pointing at the one before it, because a letter is a series by definition.</p>
		<p>It ends with the signup, for whoever arrived from a forwarded link and has not subscribed. That is most of the people who will ever read it.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Do not paywall the archive.</strong> It is the argument for subscribing.</li>
			<li><strong>Keep the number in the title tag</strong> as well as on the page — "Field Notes 042: …" is how somebody finds it again.</li>
			<li><strong>One call to action.</strong> The rail's Join and the footer's signup are the same ask twice; on a real theme, pick one.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
